            <ArticleTitle>Angio-Seal™ Embolization: A Rare Etiology of an Acute Distal Limb Ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9613863</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2017/9613863</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We herein report a serious vascular complication of diagnostic cardiac catheterization due to an embolization of an Angio-Seal closure device causing acute lower limb ischemia. The Angio-Seal was deployed via the right femoral artery following the catheterization which embolized several hours later to the right popliteal artery. Fogarty embolectomy restored perfusion to the right lower limb; however, compartment syndrome subsequently developed which required evacuation of a hematoma and repair of right popliteal artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
